# Line endings.
#
# No repo-wide normalization on purpose: flipping every file would rewrite the
# working tree for existing clones. Only the paths below are pinned, because
# their content is compared byte-for-byte and CRLF breaks them.
#
# These use explicit `text` rather than `text=auto`: with `auto`, git declined to
# normalize CRLF on checkin here, so the churn survived. Patterns are scoped by
# extension instead of by directory so a binary asset dropped into one of these
# trees later is not mangled.

# Read as raw text and asserted verbatim -- agents.test.ts checks that a served
# agent starts with "---\nname: greeter\n", which a CRLF checkout fails.
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.md   text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.ts   text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.json text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/test/fixtures/**/*.txt  text eol=lf

# Committed build output, vendored in from the plugin-docs-web build. The source
# index.html is pinned too because it is vite's input: with a CRLF input, vite
# emits CRLF and leaves a stray CR at its script-injection point, so every
# Windows build produced a diff against identical content.
@quartal/plugin-docs-web/index.html     text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.html        text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.js          text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.css         text eol=lf
@quartal/plugin/static/**/*.json        text eol=lf
